            Paragraph(Text("boundedAttachment starts with an actual strong certificate for K and outside nonempty tops with full proper boundaries in K. All new top sizes are at most M, and each old critical size is at least M. When there are no old criticals the latter condition is vacuous; for empty new H choose M=0. The existing forward scan constructs emitted and skipped subsequences in ORIGINAL order. skipped_upper_bound proves the propagated upper-size invariant using absence from each current original source. Consequently the new core, old core plus skipped upper simplices, excludes every old critical top. The new proper boundaries survive in that core. restrictSequence removes old critical tops from the standalone replay DOMAIN, preserving every ordered lower/upper pair. The separate replay then ends at the old core and appends its old C-only list. The two extraction theorems state exact list equality: emitted main, and skipped followed by old separate. Nothing is reversed or interleaved. No claim is made that the sufficient size bound is necessary, and no output for the enlarged family is assumed.")),
